{"id": "lg_display-2026-07-29-015", "date": "2026-07-29", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 31, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": ["lg_display", "jdi", "lg_elec"], "customers": ["lg_elec"], "suppliers": ["lg_display"]}, "topics": ["oled_penetration"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.9, "reasons": ["多公司提及", "供應鏈上下游同時提及"]}, "title": "LG Display to brand its maskless OLED production process as FLiPP", "content": "<p>Last year, we <a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/lg-display-looking-adopting-jdis-eleap-maskless-deposition-technology-its-oled\">reported</a> that LG Display is looking into adopting <a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/japan-display\">Japan Display</a>'s eLEAP technology at its OLED TV production lines in Paju, perhaps seeking to produce RGB AMOLED displays for IT applications at these fabs that are currently under utilized. In April 2026, we <a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/lg-display-advanc", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/lg-display-brand-its-maskless-oled-production-process-flipp", "type": "rss"}]}
